  "body": {
    "id": "prop:janvin-subclass-sharp-transfer",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "For every fixed observable distribution of \\(O\\) and every sustained-arm full-data extension admitted by \\(\\mathfrak M_H\\), restriction to \\(\\mathfrak M_H^{\\mathrm J}\\) leaves the conditional identified set of \\((B,T,W)\\) exactly \\(\\mathcal G_H(p_{BT},q)\\), and its \\((B,W)\\) projection exactly \\(\\Gamma_H(p,q)\\). Consequently the endpoints in \\(\\text{thm:sharp-threshold-endpoints}\\), the complete value set and support function in \\(\\text{thm:joint-value-set-and-support}\\), and the deterministic and randomized shared-law regret and minimax correspondences are sharp without change on the published raw no-carry-over subclass intersected with \\(B+W\\le H\\). Both inclusions hold at Hall equalities, and no raw count is bounded by \\(H\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "O",
      "\\mathfrak M_H",
      "\\mathfrak M_H^{\\mathrm J}",
      "H",
      "\\mathcal G_H(p_{BT},q)",
      "p_{bt}",
      "q_w",
      "B",
      "T",
      "W",
      "\\Gamma_H(p,q)",
      "J_m"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:janvin-raw-no-carryover-subclass",
      "def:response-tree-handle",
      "lem:cap-fibre-mixture",
      "thm:causal-response-tree-lift",
      "lem:triple-projection-and-extension",
      "thm:sharp-threshold-endpoints",
      "thm:joint-value-set-and-support",
      "def:randomized-shared-law-regret",
      "thm:randomized-minimax-regret"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Fix the observable distribution and the stipulated sustained-arm extension. Let \\(\\Theta_{\\gamma}^{\\mathrm J}\\) denote the set of conditional laws of \\((B,T,W)\\) among intensive survivors generated by laws in \\(\\mathfrak M_H^{\\mathrm J}\\) with that observable distribution and sustained-arm extension.\n\nFor the first inclusion, \\(\\mathfrak M_H^{\\mathrm J}\\subseteq\\mathfrak M_H\\) by \\(\\text{def:janvin-raw-no-carryover-subclass}\\). The converse direction of \\(\\text{thm:causal-response-tree-lift}\\) therefore gives\n\\[\n \\Theta_{\\gamma}^{\\mathrm J}\\subseteq\\mathcal G_H(p_{BT},q). \\tag{1}\n\\]\nThis step uses landmark-survival positivity for conditioning, capped residual transportability for the \\(W\\) margin, and capped capacity for the support restriction, exactly as verified in that theorem.\n\nFor the reverse inclusion, take any \\(\\gamma\\in\\mathcal G_H(p_{BT},q)\\). The forward construction in \\(\\text{thm:causal-response-tree-lift}\\) preserves the observable distribution and sustained-arm extension and realizes \\(\\gamma\\). Its cap-fibre calculation applies \\(\\text{lem:cap-fibre-mixture}\\) conditionally on the two survivor populations and gives\n\\[\n \\mathcal L(Y_K^{1\\to0}-Y_k^{1\\to0}\\mid S_k^1=1)\n =\\mathcal L(Z\\mid S_k^0=1).                              \\tag{2}\n\\]\nEquation (2), together with membership in \\(\\mathfrak M_H\\), is precisely membership in \\(\\mathfrak M_H^{\\mathrm J}\\). Hence\n\\[\n \\mathcal G_H(p_{BT},q)\\subseteq\\Theta_{\\gamma}^{\\mathrm J}. \\tag{3}\n\\]\nCombining (1) and (3) proves equality. By \\(\\text{lem:triple-projection-and-extension}\\), projecting this equality onto \\((B,W)\\) gives exactly \\(\\Gamma_H(p,q)\\).\n\nEvery threshold value is the affine map\n\\[\n J_m=\\pi\\left\\{\\sum_{b<m}\\mu_b+\n                  \\sum_{b\\ge m,w}wx_{bw}\\right\\}.       \\tag{4}\n\\]\nTherefore equality of the plan set implies equality of every coordinate range and of the full vector image. The attainment argument in \\(\\text{thm:sharp-threshold-endpoints}\\) makes the displayed endpoints sharp, while \\(\\text{thm:joint-value-set-and-support}\\) identifies the full image, its support function, and deterministic regret from that same plan set. Finally, \\(\\text{thm:randomized-minimax-regret}\\) expresses randomized regret entirely through the same support function, so its regret and minimax correspondence are unchanged as well. None of these arguments invokes strict Hall slack. The cap-fibre at \\(w=H\\) can contain arbitrarily large raw residuals, so equality of the capped plan sets introduces no global raw-count bound.",
    "justification": "This proves maximality relative to the published raw no-carry-over restriction: adding it does not shrink any capped coupling, endpoint, joint value, or regret set.",
    "gap": "Without the cap-fibre construction, sharpness under the broader capped model would not imply sharpness on the published uncapped residual-equality subclass.",
    "consumer": "The comparison with JanvinRyalenSarvetStensrud2025 can be stated as an exact sharp extension rather than only as a capped analogue.",
